---@alias paypal.customer_disputes_v1.OfferTypeList paypal.customer_disputes_v1.OfferType[]

---The JSON patch object to apply partial updates to resources.
---@class paypal.customer_disputes_v1.Patch
---@field op paypal.customer_disputes_v1.PatchOp|string The operation.
---@field path? string The <a href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6901">JSON Pointer</a> to the target document location at which to complete the operation.
---@field value? any The value to apply. The <code>remove</code>, <code>copy</code>, and <code>move</code> operations do not require a value. Since <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc69021">JSON Patch</a> allows any type for <code>value</code>, the <code>type</code> property is not specified.
---@field from? string The <a href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6901">JSON Pointer</a> to the target document location from which to move the value. Required for the <code>move</code> operation.

---@class paypal.customer_disputes_v1.PatchDisputeRequest
---@field id string The ID of the dispute for which to provide the supporting information.
---@field body? paypal.customer_disputes_v1.PatchRequest

---@class paypal.customer_disputes_v1.PatchDisputeResponse

---The operation.
---@alias paypal.customer_disputes_v1.PatchOp "add"|"remove"|"replace"|"move"|"copy"|"test"

